---
title: Turkey gravy
servings: 12
yield: 4 cups
tags: [american, thanksgiving, holiday]
cuisine: american
time: 15 minutes
source: Turkey Gravy by Nagi Maehashi, RecipeTin Eats, https://www.recipetineats.com/turkey-gravy/
---

> Make this in the pan from Roast turkey (mains/poultry) while the bird rests.

Set the #roasting pan{} over medium heat with 6 tbsp of the turkey drippings and the garlic and onion still in it.

When it sizzles, stir in the @all-purpose flour{6%tbsp} and cook ~{1%minute}, stirring all the time.

Pour in the @chicken broth{4%cups}(low-sodium) a little at a time, whisking until smooth.

Simmer until it is as thick as you like; it thickens more as it cools. Season with @salt{} and @black pepper{}.

Strain into a jug through a #fine-mesh sieve{}, pressing on the solids, and discard them. Keep it warm in a #thermos{} until serving.
